cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Colony Counter: an explainable, human-in-the-loop tool for microbial colony counting on gridded and plain agar plates"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Arnold
    family-names: William
repository-code: "https://github.com/williamarnold708/colony-counter"
abstract: >-
  An open-source tool for counting microbial colonies from plate photographs
  under real laboratory conditions, developed to solve a quality-control need
  in a brewery microbiology lab. It combines a trained object-detection model
  with a classical computer-vision fallback (including grid-line inpainting for
  printed counting plates) and a human-in-the-loop correction interface.
  Corrections made while counting can be saved back into the training dataset,
  so the model improves on the cases an analyst had to fix. A bundled labelling
  tool and training pipeline let any lab build a detector from its own plates.
keywords:
  - colony counting
  - microbiology
  - quality control
  - brewing
  - object detection
  - computer vision
  - human-in-the-loop
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-20"
